WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.520
Westworld Season 2 Episode 5 begins in the
week ahead timeline.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.110
Strand’s forces are “draining” the flooded
valley, and fishing out the dead hosts – bringing

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.760
them to the Mesa Hub to try’n fix them and
recover their code.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.240
But Antoine finds that a third of the host
brains are empty.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.419
Not like they’re “wiped”, but “Like
they never held data to begin with” . So

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:23.929
did someone put new empty brains in these
hosts?

00:00:23.929 --> 00:00:25.770
What happened to their old brains?

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:30.710
Maybe these empty hosts are decoys, and Dolores
put their real brains in new bodies, so they

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.320
can escape Westworld – like how Maeve got
a new body to remove the explosive in her

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.170
spine last season . Dolores said she’d use
the valley as “a weapon” , so maybe these

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:43.030
hosts in the valley are part of her plan.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:48.270
We also see more of the Cradle – a kind
of “simulation technology” or “time

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.270
capsule”.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:53.550
Someone has destroyed the “hosts' backups”
it held . If the hosts no longer have backups,

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.691
maybe it’s now possible for them to permanently
die – and like William they’re in real

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:03.120
danger for the first time .
Strand makes a weird comment about someone

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.109
giving “quite a story” . He might mean
Ford’s story.

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:11.049
At least some of what’s happening this season
seems to be part of Ford’s last narrative

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:15.329
– he said there’d be “violence” and
“Surprises” and “the birth of a new

00:01:15.329 --> 00:01:20.420
people” . Both Bernard and William say they’re
in Ford’s “game” . But Strand looks

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:26.130
at Bernard and talks about figuring out “how
the story turns” . Like in Episode 1, it

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:31.130
seems like Strand is trying to get information
out of Bernard . What does he think Bernard

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.130
knows?

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.499
Something about Peter Abernathy, or James
Delos?

00:01:34.499 --> 00:01:37.430
Or Ford, and the general Skynet shitstorm?

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.709
Does Strand know that Bernard is a host?

00:01:40.709 --> 00:01:42.259
Bernie is acting weird.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:46.859
There are theories that this Bernard is actually
a human-host clone of Arnold , or that this

00:01:46.859 --> 00:01:51.950
whole week-ahead timeline is a simulation
in the Cradle to interrogate Bernard.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:56.340
At this point we still don’t know, but something
is up here.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.569
In the previous week timeline, Teddy and Dolores
arrive at Sweetwater.

00:02:00.569 --> 00:02:04.639
Teddy calls this place “home” , because
he and Dolores lived here for thirty years.

00:02:04.639 --> 00:02:10.300
But Dolores says it’s not really home . They
see Clementine meeting the new host that took

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:15.230
over her role after Clem was decommissioned
– she says the same scripted lines that

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.120
Clem said in her loop.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.800
So this is proof of the fakeness of life in
Sweetwater . And if their lives were fake,

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.730
is Dolores and Teddy’s relationship real?

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.410
They go to a field where they used to dream
of running away together “Someday” . But

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:33.680
after thirty years in their loops, “Someday”
never came.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.939
Now that they’re “free”, Teddy asks
Dolores to finally go start a life together

00:02:37.939 --> 00:02:44.120
. But Dolores feels she has to stay and fight
her war against humans . In a way, her wokeness

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:50.620
makes her less free – she feels more responsibility
now than she did as an ignorant machine.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:55.550
But Dolores does decide that her love for
Teddy is real , and they have sex, maybe for

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:58.900
the first time in their thirty year relationship.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.160
But it might also be their last time.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.850
Dolores has a weird metaphor about burning
weak cows to stop a spreading sickness . The

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:14.230
point is she thinks Teddy is too nice to survive
the war ahead . Like, in Episode 3, Teddy

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.730
let Craddock go free – then Craddock went
on a killing spree in Las Mudas.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.150
Teddy’s mercy is dangerous.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:25.510
And with this sickness metaphor, it sounds
like Dolores is worried that Teddy’s compassion

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.060
might spread.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:32.830
So Dolores uses her human tech, Phil, to “Overwrite”
Teddy’s personality.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:37.900
The changes are so “extreme” that Phil
says Teddy might not survive . These shots

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:43.400
from a pre-release of the episode show Teddy’s
personality before and after – Dolores maxes

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.530
out his aggression and cruelty, and sets his
empathy to zero.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:53.350
These shots might not be canon, but the point
is Dolores destroys the man Teddy was – she

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:59.170
sacrifices the one she loves for the sake
of her war, like Stannis with Shireen.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:04.290
As Maeve argued earlier, it seems hypocritical
for Dolores to kill and control people when

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:09.910
she claims to be fighting for freedom . Dolores
says this is the only way , and that she knows

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:15.210
“how this story ends” . So maybe she’s
got some master plan, with the Valley and

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.549
these hosts – and the death of Teddy.

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:23.840
But even if this wins her war, is it worth
her becoming like the enemy she’s fighting

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.040
against?

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.870
Dolores prepares the Westworld train to go
to the Mesa Hub and rescue her host father

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.660
Peter , who was taken by Charlotte in Episode
3.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.300
After Dolores’ brutality towards Teddy,
you gotta wonder if Dolores is helping Peter

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:43.240
out of love, or if she just needs the data
in his head for her plan.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.240
Maeve and co.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.400
get captured by samurai hosts from Shogunworld.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:51.440
Maeve uses her voice commands on them, but
they don’t work cause the Shogun hosts only

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.550
know Japanese . That would also explain why
these Ghost Nation hosts were immune earlier

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:57.070
– they speak Lakota.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:02.350
But Lee says that all hosts have many languages
buried in their code – which’ll come in

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:03.820
handy later on.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:09.430
Lee says Shogunworld is like Westworld, but
more violent, and Japanese , so rich weebs

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:11.100
can wave katanas around.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.590
Which doesn’t seem very safe – Westworld’s
guns are one thing, but it must be hard to

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.919
stop guests hurting themselves with swords
and things.

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:24.230
We learn that Lee copied bits of Shogunworld
off Westworld . So there’s a town like Sweetwater,

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.880
with a place like the Mariposa Saloon.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.760
The hosts Akane and Sakura are based on Maeve
and Clementine.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.540
And the hosts Musashi and Hanaryo rob Akane’s
tea house, just like Hector and Armistice

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.260
robbed Maeve’s saloon.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:41.350
Lots of these shots are direct recreations
of the Westworld originals.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:46.889
So this is a classic Westworld brainfuck,
using repetition to make us question identity

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:51.480
– what does it mean to be Maeve when there’s
a Japanese copy of her?

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:56.100
It also reflects the long history of Japanese
samurai films and Westerns borrowing from

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:00.419
each other . Musashi’s actor says it’s
“beautiful” the way East and West used

00:06:00.419 --> 00:06:06.610
each other’s ideas . And yet HBO keeps restricting
our videos for copyright, so go figure.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:10.600
The Westworld hosts have mixed reactions to
their “doppel-bot[s]”.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.440
Hector doesn’t trust Musashi.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.380
Armistice and Hanaryo snake-charm each other.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.690
And Maeve sees herself in Akane.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:22.350
Akane’s motherly relationship with Sakura
is similar to Maeve’s relationships with

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.660
Clementine and with her daughter.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:29.389
So when Akane kills to protect Sakura from
the Shogun’s men, Maeve decides to help

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.389
her.

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:34.590
That night, the group is attacked by the Shogun’s
ninjas, who abduct Sakura.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:39.240
Maeve has visions and hears voices – she
seems to be tapping in to the “mesh network”

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:44.150
Bernard mentioned – a subconscious link
between nearby hosts . It’s like Maeve is

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.670
psychic and can hack hosts with her mind.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:52.070
So she uses this “voice” power to control
and kill a ninja . When the Shogun’s army

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:57.110
arrives, Hector Musashi Armistice and Hanaryo
make a distraction so Maeve and Akane can

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:02.520
escape – turns out Maeve wasn’t kidding
about leaving Hector for dead . Lee questions

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:06.790
whether Maeve should risk herself to help
Akane and Sakura, arguing that they’re just

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:12.360
machines . But Maeve says her choices and
love are more than just code . On the way

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:17.180
to save Sakura, we see Delos security have
been slaughtered by Shogunworld hosts . Which

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.840
is… impressive.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:24.300
Like, the battle of Fort Forlorn Hope was
one thing – those hosts had guns and nitro.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:29.370
But the Shogun hosts have swords – and somehow
they beat Delos security who have assault

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:35.170
rifles . They also have walkie talkie thingies
– Lee takes one from a corpse.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:39.260
Maybe he’s planning to betray Maeve, and
rejoin the humans.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:40.260
Maeve and co.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:43.419
pretend to be a Chinese envoy, and go meet
the Shogun.

00:07:43.419 --> 00:07:47.340
The Shogun’s off his loop, but not cause
he’s woke – he’s just “broken”,

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:52.350
leaking brain fluid like Bernard was . Akane
shows herself to the Shogun, who is shocked

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:56.810
that she’d risk her life for Sakura instead
of running away . It’s just like how Maeve

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:01.360
risks her life to rescue her daughter instead
of leaving Westworld last season.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:05.830
The Shogun agrees to release Sakura, if Akane
dances for him.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:10.270
That night, Maeve and Akane find the Shogun
has carved the shape of “A cherry blossom

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:12.130
tree” into Sakura’s back.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:17.970
The name Sakura means cherry blossom in Japanese
. Akane and Maeve talk about their shared

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:23.140
scripted story of a “new world” which
represents freedom to them . Maeve uses her

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:28.540
voice power and offers to wake Akane, show
her the truth behind her simulated world.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:35.229
But Akane refuses – and Maeve respects her
choice, so Akane can keep her grief for Sakura’s

00:08:35.229 --> 00:08:40.050
pain . Which kind of implies that love and
grief are illusions that Akane might lose

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.050
if she awoke.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:47.170
But the way Maeve lets Akane choose contrasts
with Dolores forcing Teddy to her will.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:52.680
Though these might both be paths to consciousness
– a big theme of last season is that suffering

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:58.370
leads hosts to awakening . Dolores makes Teddy
suffer, and says “we all need to suffer”

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:02.890
“To grow” . And Maeve lets Akane choose
to feel Sakura’s pain.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:08.020
These two different paths might reflect how
Maeve and Dolores themselves first became

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:11.670
conscious – Maeve chose to get off that
train.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:17.570
But Dolores’ awakening with Ford was suspiciously
similar to her coded killing of Arnold.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.960
Is Dolores really free?

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.180
The stage is set for Akane’s dance.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:27.370
In the background, these banners show symbols
of Westworld, the maze and the Delos data

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:32.290
project – cause the best way to hide a conspiracy
is to show its symbol everywhere.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:36.470
The Shogan kills Sakura – to the horror
of Akane and Maeve.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:41.339
Of course, they could probably resurrect Sakura,
like Dolores raised Craddock – but maybe

00:09:41.339 --> 00:09:44.570
Sakura’s death is more meaningful if it’s
final.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:49.800
In Episode 1, Arnold said that something’s
real when it’s “irreplaceable” . Akane

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:54.940
performs her dance, and ends it by ripping
off the Shogun’s head – kind of like in

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:55.940
Zoolander.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:10:00.620
The title of this episode is “Akane no Mai”,
which can mean Akane’s dance.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:06.190
But Akane also means deep red . And this is
a bloody red dance.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:10.350
Just before the Shogun’s men kill Maeve,
she unlocks her mutant power and reaches into

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:13.850
the Matrix and makes all of the Shogun’s
men kill each other.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:17.430
With her new power, Maeve can control all
hosts.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:22.170
She says she “found a new voice”, and
“Now we use it” . And then she picks up

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:23.250
a sword.

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:27.290
But maybe Maeve will use her power for something
more than killing.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:32.430
Before, we saw Maeve use her voice power to
lead Akane towards consciousness.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:34.960
Maeve’s power can wake hosts.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:39.080
And the way Bernard described the mesh network,
a message can be sent to nearby hosts, who

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:44.330
spread the message to yet more hosts – if
Maeve’s voice works through this network,

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:48.790
maybe Maeve could chain wake hundreds of hosts
at once.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:54.360
So Westworld continues to ask complex questions
about freedom and control, consciousness and

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:55.380
identity.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.980
Who what and when is Bernard?

00:10:57.980 --> 00:10:59.670
Is Ford still in control?

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:01.270
What’s happening at the valley?

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:03.779
Is it okay for Dolores to control hosts?

00:11:03.779 --> 00:11:06.110
Are Dolores and Teddy’s lives real?

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:08.930
What does it mean to be you if there are two
yous?

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.649
And what’s the right way use a magic wifi
superpower?

00:11:12.649 --> 00:11:13.790
Thanks for watching.

